=== intro

A message arrives, encrypted: "I know what you carry. Meet me at the Vermillion Lounge if you want to know what it means."

The Vermillion is upscale—silk and synth-wood, drinks that cost a day's wages. A figure in the corner booth waves you over. Old. Wealthy. Eyes too bright.

"Prior artifacts," they whisper. "I've been collecting since before the Silence. I know things the Collective would kill for."

* [Listen to what they know]
  ~ flag met_collector
  ~ chronicle "The Collector"
    Met a Prior artifact collector. What they told us... we're still processing.
  -> revelation

* [Leave—this feels like a trap]
  ~ chronicle "Declined Meeting"
    Turned down a meeting with someone who claimed to know about Prior artifacts. Trust is expensive.
  -> END

=== revelation

"The Silence wasn't a failure," they say, leaning close. "It was a shutdown. Someone—something—turned the Beacons off. All at once. Across the entire galaxy."

They tap the table. "The question isn't what happened. It's why. And whether it will happen again."

They slide a data chip across to you. "Routes to places the charts don't show. Worth more than credits."

* [Take the chip]
  ~ flag collector_data
  ~ chronicle "Hidden Routes"
    Received coordinates from a Prior collector. Places the charts don't show. Whether we'll use them remains to be seen.
  -> END

* [Refuse—some knowledge is dangerous]
  ~ morale += 5
  ~ chronicle "Dangerous Knowledge"
    Refused data from a Prior collector. Some doors are better left closed.
  -> END
